{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/916359-a-npc-antagonist-template-for-people-to-use","id":916359,"title":"A NPC antagonist template for people to use","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T12:25:24-07:00","id":916359,"title":"A NPC antagonist template for people to use","content":"<b>Serial Killer</b><br /> <b>Breed:</b> homid<br /> <b>auspice: </b>ragabash<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>Oh, so pretty and so cute, I will have fun cutting you </i><i>open..</i><br /> <br /> <b>History: </b>You were always different from other kids, and you knew it quite well. Your overworked mother could not watch you rip the wings of flies, and you never knew your father. Growing up without the concept of remorse, and alone made you a loner and a creep to other kids. They knew you were 'off', and your low Rage was not the reason.<br /> <br /> Your change came when you were finally confronted by your neighbourhood kids, the idiots were killed easily by your crinos claws. You approached te change as a gift from the heavens, after all, now humans too were easily your prey.<br /> <br /> You could have joined any tribe, but you cared very little for their 'holy war', especially when you figured out your 'fun' was considered tainted. You instead opted out to become rabble. Barely a rited Bone Gnawer, you could come and go as you pleased.<br /> <br /> Now you hunt. You refuse to kill fellow homeless, after all, what is the sport in that? No, you go for the rich socialites that live alone. Even with you limited abilities as a cliath, you are easily better than them.<br /> Concept: You do not care about the Wyrm, you consider it to be just a silly story the garou tell themselves to not see the truth. You do. You are a monster without peer. While your tribal status should by all rights put you on the streets, you live quite pleasantly off your victims. You are by no means reckless or stupid, the spirits have given you the gifts of stealth and you use them eagerly.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying hints:</b> Be polite and respectful at the moots, do not make any waves. You know you are good, but you can as easily be caught if you kill the wrong person. Refuse most contact with other garou, you do not feel the urge to be in a pack at all and they would just be in the way.<br /> Lately, you have gotten messages from Black Spiral Dancers, offering you a place in their tribe. You have refused, they are just another group of idiots to you. Your arrogance will surely one day be your undoing...<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment: </b>knives, shabby clothes, numerous apartment keys.<br /> <br /> <b>Using this character: </b>The Serial Killer is a great antagonist for a cliath pack. He works alone and is not interested in the Wyrm, yet reeks of it. The Killer is a true sociopath, caring only for himself. His downfall is, that he lacks any knowledge of the Garou Nation beyond the very basics. He has no idea what kinfolk are, or that garou have multiple breeds.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T10:27:19-07:00","id":916891,"title":"","content":"It's great. In my chronicles, there is problem of Garou being serial killers because of their Rage. However, usually it is a result of Lunatics who resisted the change, rather than someone who has changed. Good use of the Rabble among the Bone Gnawers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:51:53-07:00","id":917432,"title":"","content":"Not a singular garou, but rather a group this time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Currs</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> The Garou Nation can often hardly be called an open society. While it accepts women far better than most human cultures, it is still a xenophobic and closed minded society. And as people grow farther and farther away from the old ways, and the old ways are exposed as harmful, learning to accept the change to Garou Nation becomes harder and harder.<br /> <br /> For some, the Nation's culture is too alien. No matter how desperate the fight against the Wyrm, it cannot justify killing innocents, treating kinfolk poorly or the rampant ableism. Not to mention the brainwashing most cubs go through. These garou turn against their own, trying to destroy the monsters they have been exposed to.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> The name Curr is a term these garou are referred to by the Nation, since most Currs do not reveal their true intentions to anyone. They would not truly take on labels anyway, as they reject the Nation's poisonous dogma and that includes the vocabry.<br /> <br /> While there are some who reject the Nation because they wish to revel in their monstrous natures, most Currs only wish to save humanity from the Garou Nation. As such, most tend to avoid any strategy that might get people killed. Instead, they try to get the garou destroyed by exposing them in various ways. Animal abuse, murder, fraud and other expositions of crimes are common.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are those who are willing to bring the Nation down in a blaze of glory. Trying to destroy a sept through bombing or undoing wards. Or just facing their elders openly. These Currs rarely survive to become cliath. Those who do tend to be subtle, diverting attention away from themselves as much as possible. They tend anoymously report any raids or break ins their sept's garou might plan.<br /> <br /> Each Curr has their own reason to reject the Nation, and since they do not communicate with each other (or are even aware of others like them), they tend to vary wildly. To some, they see the Nation as a dangerous cult. Others might see the presence of lupus garou and kinfolk as animal abuse and most do see homid kinfolk as abuse victims as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller hints: </b>The Currs mean well. In fact, most have legimate points about the Garou Nation. Their downfall is that they cannot see or accept that the Wyrm has a legimate hold on human authorities and organizations. As each Curr is a true lone wolf, they often die before they can figure this out. As such, they end up hurting the people they seek to protect.<br /> <br /> The Currs are not strawmen who are ignorant of shades of gray and should not be used as such. Their purpose is to show how alien and flawed the Garou Nation is, and yet how its methods have a reason behind them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}